Original commit body from d0c88d36f8abfc06c66a7b25ebfbd634fe08c264:

Six analyzers left their functions, macros and methods at stable_id=None
for the ADR-0035 backstop floor, which nulls every same-name group in a
file (a multimethod's defmethods, a generic's methods, an R name
reassigned to a function of another arity). Each now mints the producer
formula at construction through overload_arity.declared_arity_stable_id:

- erlang: name/arity with meta["arity"] (the callback_stable_id inputs,
  minus the abstract decorator); -define(NAME(A, B)) macros record their
  arguments in meta["parameters"].
- clojure: ns-qualified name; a defmethod's dispatch value appended
  (whitespace/commas collapsed); a multi-arity form stays one node whose
  arity bodies merge into one parameter list (extra arities as defaults,
  & rest as the variadic entry); defmulti takes the zero-parameter formula.
- commonlisp: package::name (latest in-package); lambda-list sections
  mapped to parameter entries; a defmethod's specializers are parameter
  types (typed tier) and its qualifiers the decorators slot.
- r: parameters from function(...) (defaults, ... variadic); scope chain
  outer/inner over enclosing named functions.
- cmake, gnuplot: named arguments / dummy variables as parameters.

Floor/null -> producer only: every previously producer-computed id is
byte-identical on the gate fixtures and a corpus sample (erlang 59 files,
clojure 60, r 80, cmake 60, gnuplot 2). Baseline: the six languages leave
floor_and_null and sibling_deletion_moves.

Carry-overs: base.py's floor-collision example and beam_behaviour.py no
longer describe Elixir per-clause symbols. The producer-axis ratchet's
value_flow typed `x.kind` as every module-local record with a `kind`
field; it now honours the receiver's own declaration (an annotated
parameter/assignment, or a loop over a collection annotated list[C]),
and a receiver declared as a foreign class is unresolvable rather than
the union. elixir.py drops its workaround (kind = key.kind). The
route-producer scanner in test_depends_on_producer_sets no longer counts
a stable_id helper's decorators= keyword as a meta write.

